	(text "DIN inputs: two isolated digital inputs (DIN1, DIN2) through optocouplers"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 12.7 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "633632fc-c849-5c5c-8f04-23b685d935fb")
	)
	(text_box "WHAT IT DOES\nTwo digital inputs for vehicle signals of 9-36 V: DIN1 = engine running (alternator L / D+ or oil-pressure switch), DIN2 = pulse counter.\nAn input is active when it is more than about 6.7 V above DIN COM (VEH_GND). Each input lights the LED inside an optocoupler (U301, U302);\nthe ESP32 only sees the optocoupler's transistor. The two sides share no copper, so a ground offset or a spike on the vehicle wire cannot reach the logic.\nVEH_GND is NOT the board GND: it is the inputs' own return wire (DIN COM), joined to nothing on this board except the optocoupler LEDs.\n\nPINS OF THIS MODULE (its block on the top sheet)\nDIN1_RAW (in): J1 pin 15: input 1 (alternator / ignition / oil pressure), 0-36 V\nDIN2_RAW (in): J1 pin 16: input 2 (pulses, up to 1 kHz), 0-36 V\nVEH_GND: J1 pins 7 and 8 (DIN COM): the isolated return of both inputs\nDIN1_IN_N (out): to ESP32 GPIO27; low = input 1 active (the _N means active low)\nDIN2_IN_N (out): to ESP32 GPIO26; low = input 2 active\n+3V3 (in): supply for the pull-ups (logic side only)\nGND: board ground (logic side only)\nPower and ground reach the parts on this sheet only through these pins: the ground and supply symbols drawn on this sheet are local to it."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 17.78 0)
		(size 388 34.75)
		(margins 1.5 1.5 1.5 1.5)
		(stroke
			(width 0.1524)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "f9ee5619-20e9-5f6e-8831-6202215d1cba")
	)
	(rectangle
		(start 190.5 71.12)
		(end 190.5 160.02)
		(stroke
			(width 0.1524)
			(type dash)
			(color 200 60 0 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(uuid "2f58262f-d6f2-5b78-95ae-bbe923a0ba42")
	)
	(text "VEHICLE SIDE (isolated)\nreturn = VEH_GND (DIN COM)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 152.4 66.08 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(color 200 60 0 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "7f012e1e-0fac-5b59-aa22-549e278ca4f4")
	)
	(text "LOGIC SIDE\nboard GND and +3V3"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 193.04 66.08 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(color 200 60 0 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "49a9f3c9-5ed5-5a9f-ab7d-7f5b3b450819")
	)
	(text "ISOLATION BARRIER (dashed line): only U301 and U302 cross it. On the PCB the DIN island is cut off by milled slots:\nkeep every vehicle-side part and track (R301-R304, D301-D302, R306-R309, D303-D304, VEH_GND) on the J1 side of the slots\nand every logic part on the other side. No track, pour or via may cross. Vehicle-side nets use the 0.8 mm Vehicle clearance."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 81.28 165.1 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(color 200 60 0 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "7f8c9f7a-a1a3-551b-87b7-a563fdce9c49")
	)
	(text_box "PARTS AND THEIR JOBS\nR301-R303, R306-R308: 1k each, three in series per input (3 kohm): limit the input current. Three 1206 resistors share the voltage and heat of a surge.\nD301, D303: M7 (1000 V) reverse block: a negative voltage or spike on the input cannot drive current backwards through the LED.\nD302, D304: BZT52C4V7S 4.7 V zener: sets the threshold. No current flows until the input is about 6.7 V above VEH_GND, so an open input or a 2 V \"L\" terminal reads idle.\nU301, U302: PC817C optocouplers: the LED (pins 1-2) on the vehicle side shines on a phototransistor (pins 3-4) on the logic side.\nR304, R309: 4.7k bleed across each LED: small leakage currents pass by the LED, so the input stays idle until a real signal arrives.\nR305, R310: 22k pull-ups: the output is high (idle) until the phototransistor pulls it low (input active).\nC301: 100 nF filter on DIN1: 22k x 100 nF = 2.2 ms, ignores short spikes on the engine-running signal.\nC302: 1 nF filter on DIN2: 22k x 1 nF = 22 us, fast enough to count pulses up to 1 kHz.\nRatings: Input current 0.9 mA at 9 V, 1.9 mA at 12 V, 5.8 mA at 24 V, 9.8 mA at 36 V. Survives +50 V / -60 V continuous."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 231 0)
		(size 230 24.5)
		(margins 1.5 1.5 1.5 1.5)
